# size 20x5
# Entering the alternate screen and staying there, with the primary screen full.
#
# The corpus needs this because the other alternate-screen cases leave, and what is on the screen
# afterwards is the primary grid - so an emulator that never clears on entry passes them both. Here
# the alternate screen is what is being looked at, and the rows the program did not write must be
# blank rather than showing what the shell left behind.
\e[H\e[2Jprimary-one\r\nprimary-two\r\nprimary-three\r\nprimary-four
\e[?1049h\e[2;1Honly-this-line
